PHASE 24 — Website Performance, Speed, and Technical Optimization

Goal:
Make the website fast, stable, and optimized for real users and search engines.

Important:
Do not redesign the website in this phase unless needed for performance. Focus on speed, loading, caching, code splitting, and technical health.

What to optimize:
- Homepage loading speed
- Pricing page speed
- Checkout flow speed
- Student/Parent dashboards
- Owner dashboard tables
- Images
- Videos
- Fonts
- JavaScript bundle size
- API response speed
- Database queries
- Mobile performance

Tasks:
- Add image optimization.
- Lazy-load non-critical images/videos.
- Avoid loading heavy dashboard data all at once.
- Add pagination for large tables.
- Add search debounce where needed.
- Add caching where safe.
- Avoid unnecessary API calls.
- Optimize database indexes for common queries.
- Split large components if needed.
- Reduce unused UI/code.
- Add loading skeletons for slow sections.
- Add error boundaries where practical.

Core Web Vitals targets:
- Fast LCP on homepage and pricing.
- Low CLS by reserving image/video sizes.
- Good INP by avoiding heavy client-side rendering.

Pages to prioritize:
1. Homepage
2. Pricing
3. Checkout
4. Student dashboard
5. Parent dashboard
6. Owner dashboard
7. Homework/scenario/review pages
8. Articles/videos pages

Acceptance criteria:
- Homepage feels fast on mobile.
- Pricing and checkout load quickly.
- Large tables use pagination or lazy loading.
- Images are optimized.
- Videos are lazy-loaded.
- No obvious layout shift.
- API calls are not duplicated unnecessarily.
- Database queries for dashboards are efficient.

Manual test checklist:
- Test homepage on mobile.
- Test pricing page.
- Test checkout.
- Test Owner dashboard with demo data.
- Test Student dashboard.
- Test Parent dashboard.
- Check browser console for errors.
- Check network tab for unnecessarily large assets.

